South Africa's Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA) is the country's primary data privacy and protection law. POPIA carries fines up to R10 million or result in criminal liability.
The CIS Critical Security Controls (CIS Controls) are a prioritized set of CIS Safeguards to defend against the most prevalent cyber attacks against systems and networks.

A managed SOC can block threats, but without audit-ready logs, reports, and incident response timelines, a client cannot prove that they took reasonable measures if a breach occurs.

Audit-ready evidence serves as a legal shield to mitigate or avoid massive POPIA fines and criminal liability by demonstrating proactive compliance. Audit-ready evidence also provides standardized, tamper-evident logs which verify that centralized log collection is active, security events are being reviewed and analysed daily, and authorized and unauthorized changes are tracked.





